      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Five Card Draw (Deuces Wild)",
          "subtitle": "Card Game",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Five Card Draw with all twos wild. Same deal and draw as standard; deuces substitute for any card. Best hand wins."
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Five Card Draw emerged as one of the oldest forms of poker and remained the best-known internationally until Texas Hold'em's rise in the late 20th century. Deuces Wild is a variation in which all four twos are wild; it is found mostly in home poker games and is typically played with players declaring their own hands rather than cards speaking for themselves."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Setup",
          "subtitle": "Table, deck, equipment, and deal",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Two to six players; six is often considered best. With seven or eight the deck may run out during the draw, so six is the usual maximum."
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Standard 52-card pack. All four deuces (twos) act as wild cards; no joker is used."
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Chips."
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "5 cards each; ante or blinds."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
